From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:45:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: host-common: Don't let bridge wakeup block D3cold

pci_host_common_d3cold_possible() walks every device below the host
bridge, Root Ports and switch ports included, and refuses D3cold when a
device has wakeup enabled but cannot signal PME from D3cold.

On a bridge, enabled wakeup does not describe a wake source of its own;
it lets wake events from the devices below reach the system. Since
commit 071e245ab749 ("PCI: Add support for PCIe WAKE# interrupt"), a
Root Port whose device tree node describes the slot's WAKE# line has
wakeup enabled by default. If that Root Port does not also advertise PME
from D3cold, the walk refuses D3cold even when the endpoint below has
wakeup disabled, so dw_pcie_suspend_noirq() leaves the link up and the
slot powered through system suspend.

Whether wakeup survives D3cold depends on the devices below the bridge,
and the walk checks each of them in turn. Apply the wakeup check only to
devices that are not bridges. The helper was widened from endpoints to
all devices when it was applied, so that a device kept in D0 by its
driver also blocks D3cold; that power state check still covers bridges.
Bridges no longer set the PME-from-D3cold flag either, which tells the
controller driver to keep a wake-capable device below powered.

On the Microsoft Surface Laptop 8, the M.2 Wi-Fi slot now powers off in
s2idle, which saves about 70 mW. The Wi-Fi card is reinitialised on
resume and reconnects.

Fixes: 1d2a29ccd3a1 ("PCI: host-common: Add pci_host_common_d3cold_possible() helper")
Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c
index a23907a875e..50561585425 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c
@@ -277,7 +277,12 @@ static int __pci_host_common_d3cold_possible(struct pci_dev *pdev,
 	if (pdev->current_state != PCI_D3hot)
 		goto exit;
 
-	if (device_may_wakeup(&pdev->dev)) {
+	/*
+	 * Bridges have wakeup enabled to forward PME from the devices below
+	 * them. Whether wakeup survives D3cold depends on those devices, which
+	 * the walk checks in turn.
+	 */
+	if (device_may_wakeup(&pdev->dev) && !pci_is_bridge(pdev)) {
 		if (!pci_pme_capable(pdev, PCI_D3cold))
 			goto exit;
 		else
-- 
